What a testament these people in this room that you're willing to sacrifice the comforts of what a normal church gathering would look like so that we can host a group of people who are in need.

240
00:25:40,640 --> 00:25:57,640
And although we make a concerted effort on this particular week, this is the type of sacrificial love that we are invited to participate in on a daily basis, laying down the comforts and desires of our own lives in order to demonstrate the love of God to those around us.

241
00:25:57,640 --> 00:26:04,640
And the thing as a pastor that I constantly want to remind people is that we do not do that out of religious duty.

242
00:26:04,640 --> 00:26:11,640
We don't sacrifice because we feel like we're going to earn something for God or we feel like he's going to be proud of us if we do.

243
00:26:11,640 --> 00:26:15,640
We sacrificially love because it's our family identity.

244
00:26:15,640 --> 00:26:20,640
As children of the everlasting father, we love because he first loved us.

245
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:26,640
And so I just constantly want to remind us that the invitation is not just to understand, but to live out.

246
00:26:26,640 --> 00:26:33,640
And we live out not because we think it's going to do something for us eternally, but because something has already been done for us.

247
00:26:33,640 --> 00:26:45,640
