00:44:31,640 --> 00:44:39,640
Because the news reports gangs, drugs, and violence in Detroit, she decides it's the last place her parents would ever look for her.

406
00:44:39,640 --> 00:44:44,640
Her second day there, she meets a man driving the biggest car she's ever seen.

407
00:44:44,640 --> 00:44:48,640
He offers a ride, buys her lunch, and finds her a place to stay.

408
00:44:48,640 --> 00:44:52,640
He gives her pills that make her feel better than she's ever felt before.

409
00:44:52,640 --> 00:44:57,640
She was right all along, she decides her parents were trying to keep her from the fun.

410
00:44:57,640 --> 00:45:01,640
A month passes, two months, a year.

411
00:45:01,640 --> 00:45:05,640
The man, she calls him boss, teaches her a few things men like.

412
00:45:05,640 --> 00:45:10,640
And she's underage, so men pay a premium.

413
00:45:10,640 --> 00:45:12,640
She lives in a penthouse and orders room service.

414
00:45:12,640 --> 00:45:15,640
Occasionally, she thinks of home, but their lives seem so boring now.

415
00:45:15,640 --> 00:45:20,640
She has a scare when she sees her picture on the back of a milk carton.

416
00:45:20,640 --> 00:45:22,640
Have you seen this child?

417
00:45:22,640 --> 00:45:26,640
But with blonde hair, makeup, and jewelry, no one would mistake her for a child.

418
00:45:26,640 --> 00:45:31,640
After a year, the first signs of illness appear and the boss turns mean.

419
00:45:31,640 --> 00:45:37,640
These days, we can't mess around, he growls, and she finds herself out on the street without a penny.

420
00:45:37,640 --> 00:45:41,640
She still turns a couple of tricks at night, but they barely cover her habit.

421
00:45:41,640 --> 00:45:47,640
When winter blows in, she sleeps on metal grates outside department stores.

422
00:45:47,640 --> 00:45:51,640
A teenage girl in downtown Detroit never relaxes her guard.

423
00:45:51,640 --> 00:45:54,640
Dark bands around her eyes, her cough worsens.

424
00:45:54,640 --> 00:45:59,640
One night, as she lies awake listening for footsteps, everything about her life looks different.

425
00:45:59,640 --> 00:46:06,640
She no longer feels like a woman of the world, but like a little girl lost in the cold, frightening city.

426
00:46:06,640 --> 00:46:08,640
Her pockets are empty.

427
00:46:08,640 --> 00:46:09,640
She's hungry.

428
00:46:09,640 --> 00:46:11,640
She needs a fix.

429
00:46:11,640 --> 00:46:15,640
She pulls her legs under her and shivers beneath cardboard.

430
00:46:15,640 --> 00:46:17,640
A memory jolts.

431
00:46:17,640 --> 00:46:19,640
May in Traverse City.

432
00:46:19,640 --> 00:46:24,640
A million cherry trees blooming, her golden retriever dashing through rows of trees.

433
00:46:24,640 --> 00:46:26,640
God, why did I leave?

434
00:46:26,640 --> 00:46:29,640
My dog eats better than I do now.

435
00:46:29,640 --> 00:46:32,640
She knows she wants to go home.

436
00:46:32,640 --> 00:46:34,640
Three calls go to voicemail.

437
00:46:34,640 --> 00:46:40,640
She hangs up twice, but the third time she says, "Dad, Mom, it's me.

438
00:46:40,640 --> 00:46:43,640
I was wondering about maybe coming home.

439
00:46:43,640 --> 00:46:45,640
I'm catching a bus up your way.

440
00:46:45,640 --> 00:46:47,640
It'll get there around midnight tomorrow.

441
00:46:47,640 --> 00:46:50,640
If you're not there, I'll just stay on the bus until it hits Canada."

442
00:46:50,640 --> 00:46:53,640
The seven-hour bus ride gives her time to reconsider.

443
00:46:53,640 --> 00:46:55,640
What if they're out of town?

444
00:46:55,640 --> 00:46:56,640
What if they don't check their voicemail?

445
00:46:56,640 --> 00:46:58,640
What if they've written her off as dead?

446
00:46:58,640 --> 00:47:02,640
Her thoughts bounce between fear and the speech that she rehearses.

447
00:47:02,640 --> 00:47:04,640
She says, "Dad, I'm sorry.

448
00:47:04,640 --> 00:47:05,640
I know I was wrong.

449
00:47:05,640 --> 00:47:07,640
Can you forgive me?"

450
00:47:07,640 --> 00:47:10,640
She says these words over and over.

451
00:47:10,640 --> 00:47:12,640
Her throat tightening as she rehearses.

452
00:47:12,640 --> 00:47:14,640
Then she hasn't apologized to anyone in years.

453
00:47:14,640 --> 00:47:19,640
Tiny snowflakes hit the pavement.

454
00:47:19,640 --> 00:47:21,640
She's forgotten how dark it gets out here.

455
00:47:21,640 --> 00:47:22,640
Billboards appear.

456
00:47:22,640 --> 00:47:24,640
Mileage signs to Traverse City.

457
00:47:24,640 --> 00:47:25,640
Oh, God.

458
00:47:25,640 --> 00:47:29,640
When the bus rolls into the station, the brakes hiss.

459
00:47:29,640 --> 00:47:34,640
"15 minutes, folks," the driver says, "15 minutes to decide her life."

460
00:47:34,640 --> 00:47:41,640
She smooths her hair, wipes lipstick off her teeth, looks at the tobacco stains on her fingers.

461
00:47:41,640 --> 00:47:43,640
Will they notice?

462
00:47:44,640 --> 00:47:45,640
Will they even be here?

463
00:47:45,640 --> 00:47:51,640
She walks into the terminal not knowing what to expect.

464
00:47:51,640 --> 00:47:59,640
Not one of the thousand scenes she imagined prepared her for what she sees.

465
00:47:59,640 --> 00:48:06,640
There, inside the concrete walls and plastic chairs of Traverse City bus station stands a group of 40 people.

466
00:48:07,640 --> 00:48:12,640
brothers, sisters, great aunts and uncles, cousins, a grandmother and a great grandmother to boot.

467
00:48:12,640 --> 00:48:16,640
They're wearing goofy party hats and blowing noise makers.

468
00:48:16,640 --> 00:48:20,640
Taped across a wall is a banner that says, "Welcome home."

469
00:48:20,640 --> 00:48:26,640
Out of the crowd breaks her dad.

470
00:48:26,640 --> 00:48:31,640
She stares through the tears, quivering her in her eyes, and begins her speech.

471
00:48:31,640 --> 00:48:32,640
"Dad, I'm sorry, I know."

472
00:48:32,640 --> 00:48:35,640
He interrupts her.

473
00:48:36,640 --> 00:48:38,640
Hush child, we've got no time for that.

474
00:48:38,640 --> 00:48:40,640
No time for apologies.

475
00:48:40,640 --> 00:48:41,640
You'll be late for the party.

476
00:48:41,640 --> 00:48:44,640
The banquet is waiting for you at home.

477
00:48:44,640 --> 00:48:59,640
This is the type of love that Jesus demonstrates and teaches us about the everlasting Father.

478
00:48:59,640 --> 00:49:02,640
This is the type of love the Father has for you.

479
00:49:05,640 --> 00:49:09,640
He sent Jesus, the Messiah, to demonstrate and to teach you so that you might have a clearer picture,

480
00:49:09,640 --> 00:49:15,640
so that your imagination might be expanded about how much God truly loves you.

481
00:49:15,640 --> 00:49:23,640
And I don't know where you're at, or what you've done, where you've been, where you're headed.

482
00:49:24,640 --> 00:49:33,640
But I think this morning, what the Father wants to remind each of us, myself included, especially me.

483
00:49:33,640 --> 00:49:38,640
That he's a good dad.

484
00:49:38,640 --> 00:49:40,640
The perfect dad.

485
00:49:41,640 --> 00:49:42,640
That he loves us.

486
00:49:42,640 --> 00:49:43,640
That he loves us.

487
00:49:43,640 --> 00:49:48,640
And that he's inviting us to extend the love that we receive from him to others.

488
00:49:48,640 --> 00:49:55,640
We will come in contact with a number of individuals, both this week and throughout our lives.

489
00:49:56,640 --> 00:50:04,640
For those of us who have no imaginative opportunity to even grasp the reality that the God who created them might love them.

490
00:50:04,640 --> 00:50:07,640
That the God who created them might love them like this.

491
00:50:08,640 --> 00:50:12,640
And for those of us who have tasted and seen that the Lord is good.

492
00:50:13,640 --> 00:50:18,640
The first invitation is for us to continually receive that.

493
00:50:18,640 --> 00:50:21,640
That when we screw up, we turn back to the Father.

494
00:50:21,640 --> 00:50:30,640
That when we fall flat on our face, we don't look up expecting anger or frustration.

495
00:50:30,640 --> 00:50:35,640
But we look up expecting an outstretched hand picking us up and dusting us off.

496
00:50:36,640 --> 00:50:37,640
We receive it first.

497
00:50:37,640 --> 00:50:42,640
And then as we receive it, because we have first been loved by God, we go and extend that love to others.

498
00:50:42,640 --> 00:50:49,640
Hoping that in some way, shape or form, we might expand their imagination about what it means that God who created them loves them.

499
00:50:49,640 --> 00:50:55,640
We love because God first loved us.

500
00:50:55,640 --> 00:50:57,640
Let's pray.

501
00:50:57,640 --> 00:50:58,640
Father in heaven.

502
00:50:58,640 --> 00:51:04,640
Thank you for the gift of words.

503
00:51:06,640 --> 00:51:15,640
The gift of authors who can take Scripture that we've read over and over and over again and maybe even become numb to.

504
00:51:15,640 --> 00:51:22,640
And help us to reimagine what it means for you to be a compassionate Father, an everlasting Father.

505
00:51:22,640 --> 00:51:29,640
God, this morning I pray that we would have fresh eyes to see how much you truly love us.

506
00:51:31,640 --> 00:51:36,640
That we'd have fresh eyes to see how much you truly love each individual that you have created in your image.

507
00:51:36,640 --> 00:51:42,640
Individuals that frustrate us, that take advantage of us, that steal from us.

508
00:51:49,640 --> 00:51:58,640
And the invitation for those of us who are children of God is to look even at our enemies and say, you are loved by an everlasting Father.

509
00:51:58,640 --> 00:52:09,640
And because he is not yet here in the flesh, I am going to show you what his love for you looks like.

510
00:52:10,640 --> 00:52:29,640
God, help us to be a people who receive your love, who understand it emotionally, mentally, and who are able to give it out freely without fear of rejection or insecurity.

511
00:52:33,640 --> 00:52:38,640
God, I pray for each one of our guests this week.

512
00:52:38,640 --> 00:52:41,640
I pray that as we interact with them at meals.

513
00:52:41,640 --> 00:52:49,640
God, that we treat them like a child of the Most High God.

514
00:52:49,640 --> 00:52:54,640
That their imaginations might be expanded for what it means that you love them.

515
00:52:57,640 --> 00:53:02,640
God, that we might learn from them what it means that you love us.

516
00:53:02,640 --> 00:53:07,640
I pray all of this in Jesus' name.

517
00:53:07,640 --> 00:53:08,640
Amen.

518
00:53:08,640 --> 00:53:14,640
Mike, did you, I didn't talk to you.

519
00:53:14,640 --> 00:53:20,640
Do you want to give an update and share some things about where we might still need some volunteering?

520
00:53:22,640 --> 00:53:36,640
After Mike kind of gives us an update, your invitation is to go pick up your kids, hang out in the lobby, and we're going to keep the auditorium quiet for a little bit.

521
00:53:36,640 --> 00:53:44,640
And we'd invite you to spend time praying over these cots, praying a blessing over each individual that's going to stay with us throughout the week.

522
00:53:45,640 --> 00:53:50,640
We're going to bring in their bags and put them on cots and invite you to invite your children to pray with you.

523
00:53:50,640 --> 00:53:53,640
And then I'm going to hang out by the prayer tent.

524
00:53:53,640 --> 00:53:57,640
If any of you all need prayer, we'd love to do that.

525
00:53:57,640 --> 00:54:00,640
So you do what you need to do and then dismiss for that.

526
00:54:00,640 --> 00:54:02,640
Yeah, sounds good.

527
00:54:02,640 --> 00:54:04,640
Sign ups have been amazing.

528
00:54:04,640 --> 00:54:06,640
You guys have filled the blocks.

529
00:54:06,640 --> 00:54:13,640
I've got maybe my biggest need is Saturday morning getting cleaned up and church put back together.

530
00:54:14,640 --> 00:54:16,640
It starts at about 7:15.

531
00:54:16,640 --> 00:54:20,640
You can bring your kids with you on that if you want.

532
00:54:20,640 --> 00:54:23,640
This last Saturday set up, we had 25 folks.

533
00:54:23,640 --> 00:54:25,640
We finished in record time.

534
00:54:25,640 --> 00:54:26,640
It was pretty amazing.

535
00:54:26,640 --> 00:54:28,640
We've been through one cycle.

536
00:54:28,640 --> 00:54:31,640
One dinner, one night, one breakfast.

537
00:54:31,640 --> 00:54:33,640
Everything went smooth.

538
00:54:33,640 --> 00:54:35,640
You guys are rock stars with this.

539
00:54:37,640 --> 00:54:42,640
The guests and the WATS staff look forward to this week because we get it right.

540
00:54:42,640 --> 00:54:47,640
And getting it right doesn't necessarily mean that the cots aren't lined up perfectly and the coffee's hot.

541
00:54:47,640 --> 00:54:49,640
That comes with the base model.

542
00:54:50,640 --> 00:54:54,640
You guys, you love on the guests.

543
00:54:54,640 --> 00:54:56,640
And they notice.

544
00:54:56,640 --> 00:54:59,640
Thank you for that.

545
00:54:59,640 --> 00:55:02,640
Looking forward to a good week.

546
00:55:02,640 --> 00:55:05,640
If you're not signed up, just come on out.

547
00:55:05,640 --> 00:55:07,640
Just take part in the fun.

548
00:55:08,640 --> 00:55:10,640
We'll find a spot for you.

549
00:55:10,640 --> 00:55:17,640
But yeah, as you leave, if you want to pray over a cot, our guests are really struggling.

550
00:55:17,640 --> 00:55:21,640
We've got some that just have some really tough stories.

551
00:55:22,640 --> 00:55:23,640
They need Jesus.

552
00:55:23,640 --> 00:55:27,640
Just pray for them for that.

553
00:55:27,640 --> 00:55:30,640
And otherwise, that's it.

554
00:55:30,640 --> 00:55:31,640
Thank you all.

555
00:55:52,640 --> 00:55:53,640
Thank you.

556
00:55:53,640 --> 00:55:54,640
Thank you.
